Provides: x-display-manager
Description: Querencia Desktop login screen (greetd with ReGreet, alpha)
 The graphical login screen of Querencia Desktop: the greetd daemon shows
 the GTK 4 greeter ReGreet in a labwc compositor without menu or key
 bindings, with the Querencia-Klassisch theme, the Querencia icon theme
 and the background "Querencia Blau". All sessions from
 /usr/share/wayland-sessions and /usr/share/xsessions can be chosen, so
 Ubuntu (GNOME) stays available next to Querencia Desktop.
 .
 The package coexists with GDM and other display managers. It becomes the
 default display manager only when none is set up yet, when it is chosen
 in the debconf question shared/default-x-display-manager, or with
 QUERENCIA_ANMELDUNG=ja. "dpkg-reconfigure querencia-anmeldung" switches in
 both directions; removing the package restores the previous display
 manager. A running display manager is never stopped.
 .
 ReGreet 0.5.0 is built from the upstream release with its own paths
 (/etc/querencia/greetd); the configuration of the greetd package is not
 touched.
 .
 Querencia Desktop is developed with AI tools; every change is reviewed
 and accepted by the project owner.
 This is an alpha release.
